course: dictionary
lesson: 12933
title: Everlasting, and the many meanings of one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Everlasting means lasting for ever, never ending. «Her love for her grandad was everlasting.» The sentence does not say when the love will stop, so you can work out that it never will.
explain: Sometimes people use everlasting to complain. «His everlasting complaints about the rain made everyone groan.» Here everlasting means going on far too long and becoming boring. Ask yourself: is the writer talking about time, or about being annoyed?
explain: In church, hymns and the Bible, everlasting is used about God and eternal life: «God is everlasting», «everlasting life». The words around it, such as prayers and hymns, are your clues that the meaning is serious and religious.
explain: An everlasting can also be a noun, a kind of flower. «She put an everlasting in the vase.» Here the word is a name for a flower, not a description. It is a flower that keeps its shape and colour when it dries.
fact: Everlasting means lasting for ever.
fact: «Everlasting» can also mean going on far too long and boring, as in «everlasting complaints».
fact: In prayers and the Bible, «everlasting life» means life that never ends.
fact: An everlasting is a flower that keeps its shape and colour when dried.
fact: Other phrases with the same feeling are «everlasting love» and «for ever and ever».
exercise: «Her love for her grandad was everlasting.» What does everlasting mean here? | Full of noise | *Lasting for ever, never ending | Very cold | Short and quick
exercise: «His everlasting complaints about the rain made everyone groan.» What does everlasting suggest? | Happy and bright | Lasting only one day | Quiet and gentle | *Going on far too long and boring
exercise: Mia says the flowers in the vase are everlasting. What is an everlasting? | A flower that is always wet | *A flower that keeps its shape and colour when dried | A flower that only grows in winter | A flower that smells very strong
test: Which phrase uses everlasting in a prayer or Bible sentence? | Muddy shoes | Loud music | *Everlasting life | Quick lunch
test: «In the story, the sweets were everlasting gobstoppers.» How long do they last? | *For ever, never running out | For one minute | Until the next rain | Only until lunchtime
exam: «The everlasting winter in the story seemed to have no end.» What does everlasting mean here? | Warm and sunny | Very short | *Never ending | Full of colour
